     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Good news--you don&#39;t have to build devtools anymore. :-) Devtools 1.4, which supports Packrat, is available on CRAN starting yesterday, so you don&#39;t need to do the install_github dance. Just update to the version on CRAN and reload.</span><div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Jonathan.</span></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yE7bc1eKvpEJ",
   "from": "Jonathan McPherson",
   "author": "5893d17d64b5b0c2",
   "date": "2013-11-21T18:39:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: devtools not installing correctly",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I might have spoken too soon--it looks like the Mac binaries for Devtools haven&#39;t been posted yet. They should be shortly. In the meantime, I think this StackOverflow thread describes your problem and the best solution (i.e. setting make vars to indicate the compiler to use on your system):<div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19503995/error-when-with-xcode-5-0-and-rcpp-command-line-tools-are-installed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19503995/error-when-with-xcode-5-0-and-rcpp-command-line-tools-are-installed&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242962961000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0l37N_Lh4wzHqRoN98esZs\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19503995/error-when-with-xcode-5-0-and-rcpp-command-line-tools-are-installed</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Jonathan.</div></div>"
    ]
